   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In November 2018, National Confederation of Employers of Kazakhstan (NKRRK) launched a strategic plan for the period 2019-2021 and thereafter embarked on a strong implementation effort which included: Change of the statute in September 2020. The changes improved its governance structure (allowing for multiple vice presidents), enabled more inclusive membership participation (setting up regional representations) and overall improved its responsiveness to members&#x2019; needs. The addition of &quot;National&#x201D; to the name of its organization signified NKRRK&#x2019;s vision to be inclusive and representative.   
Following the targets set in its strategic plan, NKRRK revamped its visual identity in June 2021 to reflect its new structure and name. In September 2021, NKRRK also launched its new website to provide better visibility, more functionality and improved member support. 
In parallel, NKRRK built a new membership infrastructure to enhance its ability to attract and retain members. Specifically, NKRRK built a database of potential members. The database includes details of 3000 companies and is used as a springboard to increase NKRRK&#x2019;s visibility. NKRRK also adopted a membership action plan in April 2021 to increase its representation. Since the start of 2020, NKRRK recruited 30 new member companies, which are their first new members after 10 years. NKRRK renewed membership of all associations that were earlier affiliated with the Confederation. NKRRK renewed membership records for all of their members which in combination with their new database, enables them to be more responsive to their members. NKRRK used their new social network accounts to reach out to hundreds of companies (potential members) in an effort to increase their visibility and social network footprint. The increased visibility and outreach of NKRRK is evident from the increased interest of enterprises in activities organized by NKRRK. The participation in NKRRK events increased 2-3 times over the course of 2021. The ILO organized and facilitated strategic planning workshop for NKRRK in June 2018 and advised and supported them with expertise in the development of a strategic plan for (N)KRRK. The workshop was one week long and it included the staff and management of NKRRK, members of the board and member associations. The ILO also organized a training on governance for NKRRK and its member associations in November 2018 and another one on membership in May 2019. For both of these training the ILO methodology and elements of ILO EBMO toolkit were used. 
The ILO supported NKRRK with training, expert advice and know how in the development of new social networks accounts. ILO, it provided support on rebranding by providing expert advise and technical support to NKRRK in development of the new visual identity. ILO provided support in the development of the new website, including the advice and expert support in design of the architecture of the website as well as technical support in setting the site up.
In period December 2020-December 2021, the ILO provided NKRRK with advise, training and assistance in the development of its membership infrastructure. The ILO also assisted NKRRK  in using their membership infrastructure, social networks, website, databases, to increase their visibility and attracting new members.</narrative>
   </description>
